A||N||3||Eric_PA||ECM swapping 8253 to 1227148 ||||5||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||11-20-2001||04:59 PM||||Has anyone ever done this? I have a 90 3800 from a lasabre that was completely rebuilt. I would like to learn how to change the code, but can't find any support for this ECM. I have found a lot of info on the 1227148 used in the 3.8 grand nationals. I am wondering if there is any BIN file close enough to the 90 fwd 3800 to use in the 1227148 ECM. If so, then I could really mess with some things.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||11-20-2001||07:14 PM||||You need to check the DIS triggering, but it should work. The downside is that the 7148 is a C3 and is much slower (in several areas like the ALDL stream) than the 8253 which is a P4. One option is to go to the 16141470 from 91 and up.<P>Do you have a BCM and HVAC to deal with? The 7148 won't handle any of that. The 1470 will but the streams might be different enough to cause you some grief.<P>Hit me off line.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||11-20-2001||07:40 PM||||I did pick up a 16141470 from a 91 3800. the wiring is a bit different, but sounds like it would be worth the change. I'm going to check into a bit more.<BR>Thanks Terry||||reg||7
Z||000003||terryk||11-20-2001||09:01 PM||||Do you have BCM and HVAC modules that needs the data stream from the ECM? If so, you will run into problems with the 1470.  They changed the device addresses so it's unlikely the 1470 stream will work unless you luck out and the 91 stream is the same as yours.||||reg||5
